        "title": "Cycle of Life",
        "text": "Not far from the Kathmandu airport, this Hindu site is one of the \"must see\" spots in the city. Reminiscent of Varanasi, there are a number of cremation ghats along the river--all in various stages. So if you spend an hour or so, you are likely to be able to take in an entire cremation ritual. Photo ops abound, even though non-Hindus are not allowed inside the main temple. Tourists are charged a fee (but you may be able to get in if your appearance matches the locals)",
