        "title": "It's different",
        "text": "I've been to many temples back here in India, and although i dont beleive in God, it felt peaceful to visit here. We visited between 5.30 pm and 6.30 pm, which is when they do the Aarti--and the music that accompanies, kinda puts you in a trans. Further down, you can often find the priests letting go off, or burning dead bodies per some rituals, by a pond. I dont know the significance (maybe cause Yama -God of death , is a form of Lord Shiva , whose temple this is). Good to visit once. Tons of monkeys around, and photography not allowed inside.",
