        "text": "This is the most holy place in Kathmandu for Hindus and this is where cremations are ongoing. Unlike Varanasi, India, you are allowed to take pictures here. Take a guide (we found 500 NRS for 1 - 1 1/2 hrs an ok deal) to avoid feeling awkward/insecure. Evening Pooja is impressive. Stand/sit on the opposite ghats for a good view. The deer park behind the temple grounds is accessible from here but closes at 4pm already.",
